# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Softsuave Blog CMS — environment variables
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. Never commit `.env`.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Node environment (development | production | test)
NODE_ENV=development

# Public base URL of this app (used for canonical URLs, sitemap, OG, RSS).
# No trailing slash.
#
# The bare origin: this app owns the whole site — "/" is the marketing homepage,
# "/blog" the archive — so there is no mount subpath to add. It would need one
# (and `basePath` in next.config.ts to match) if the app were ever mounted under
# a subpath again: basePath prefixes routes and assets but NOT these URLs, so
# omitting it there would point every canonical one level too high.
#
# It defaults to the production origin here and in lib/env.ts, so a deployment
# that forgets the variable still publishes correct canonicals. Local dev is the
# case that opts out — uncomment the loopback line below if you want dev canonicals
# to name your own host (nothing else depends on it; the app serves the same pages
# either way).
#
#   production:  https://www.softsuave.com
#   local dev:   http://localhost:3100
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://www.softsuave.com
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3100

# ── Release flags ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Is the marketing homepage part of this deployment?
#
# The blog and the homepage are one application but ship on different dates.
# While this is false the homepage is still built and still tested — it is just
# not reachable: "/" 307s to /blog, drops out of the sitemap and breadcrumbs,
# and "home" links point at https://www.softsuave.com instead.
#
# Unset means false, so a deployment that forgets this variable hides an
# unreleased homepage rather than publishing it early. Set it to "true" (and
# rebuild — NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are baked in at build time, not read at boot)
# on the release that takes the homepage live.
NEXT_PUBLIC_HOMEPAGE_ENABLED=false

# Google Tag Manager container. Unset (or blank) loads softsuave.com's own
# container, GTM-TWMFSDC, on every page via the root layout — see src/lib/flags.ts.
# Set another ID to use that container, or `off` to disable GTM entirely
# (e.g. locally, to keep dev traffic out of the reports). Needs a rebuild.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GTM_ID=

# May search engines index this deployment? Unset (or anything but "true")
# keeps the WHOLE site noindex, nofollow: every response carries
# `X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow` and every page's robots meta agrees — see
# `siteIndexable` in src/lib/flags.ts. robots.txt still allows crawling, so
# crawlers can see the noindex. Set to "true" (and rebuild) to open the site to
# search engines.
NEXT_PUBLIC_ALLOW_INDEXING=false

# ── Database ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MySQL connection string. Matches docker-compose.yml credentials in dev.
# Host port 3307 (docker-compose maps 3307->3306) avoids clashing with a native
# MySQL that may already occupy 3306 on the host.
#
# Must start with mysql:// — a leftover postgresql:// URL from before the MySQL
# port is rejected at boot rather than failing on the first query.
#
# Never point this at a root/superuser account. The app needs only DML on its own
# schema; see README.md for the least-privilege GRANT.
DATABASE_URL=mysql://blog:blog@localhost:3307/softsuave_blog

# TLS to MySQL: verify (default) | no-verify | disable.
#   verify    — encrypts and authenticates the server. Required in production.
#               With a self-signed server cert, also set DATABASE_SSL_CA.
#   no-verify — encrypts but accepts ANY certificate, so it does not stop a
#               man-in-the-middle. A stopgap, not a configuration.
#   disable   — plaintext, credentials included. Loopback dev only.
DATABASE_SSL=disable
# PEM *contents* of the CA that signed the MySQL server certificate (not a path).
# DATABASE_SSL_CA=

# Connection-pool ceiling per process. Leave unset unless several app instances
# share one MySQL — the total must stay under the server's max_connections (151
# by default). src/lib/db.ts picks 20 at runtime and 2 during `next build`.
# DATABASE_POOL_MAX=20

# Must equal the MySQL server's innodb_ft_min_token_size. InnoDB will not index
# tokens shorter than this, so with the default of 3 a search for "AI", "UI" or
# "Go" returns nothing. docker-compose.yml sets the server to 2 to match; on a
# self-hosted server set it in my.cnf and rebuild the FULLTEXT indexes
# (`OPTIMIZE TABLE Post, Page;` with innodb_optimize_fulltext_only=ON).
SEARCH_MIN_TOKEN_SIZE=2

# ── Phone country code (optional) ─────────────────────────────
# The enquiry form preselects a calling code from the visitor's IP, falling
# back to their browser timezone, then locale, then +91. The IP step reads a
# local MaxMind GeoLite2-Country database; leave these unset and that step is
# simply skipped — the timezone fallback still works and nothing errors.
#
# To enable it: sign up free at https://www.maxmind.com/en/geolite2/signup,
# create a licence key, set it here, and run `npm run geo:update`. The database
# is not committed (see .gitignore); re-run that command monthly to refresh it.
MAXMIND_LICENSE_KEY=
GEOIP_DB_PATH=./data/GeoLite2-Country.mmdb

# ── Auth / JWT ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Secrets for signing access and refresh JWTs. MUST be long random strings in
# production (e.g. `openssl rand -base64 48`). Keep access and refresh distinct.
JWT_ACCESS_SECRET=dev-access-secret-change-me-in-production-please-0000000000
JWT_REFRESH_SECRET=dev-refresh-secret-change-me-in-production-please-000000000
# Token lifetimes (seconds). Access short-lived; refresh longer-lived.
ACCESS_TOKEN_TTL=900          # 15 minutes
REFRESH_TOKEN_TTL=2592000     # 30 days

# Secret used to sign draft preview links (signed, non-indexable).
PREVIEW_SECRET=dev-preview-secret-change-me-000000000000000000000000

# Secret token required by POST /api/v1/revalidate (on-demand ISR).
REVALIDATE_SECRET=dev-revalidate-secret-change-me-0000000000000000000000

# ── Object storage ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Driver: `local` (dev, writes to disk), `s3` (prod: Cloudflare R2 / AWS S3 /
# MinIO) or `cloudinary` (prod: Cloudinary image CDN).
STORAGE_DRIVER=local

# Local driver: directory (relative to project root) files are written to,
# and the public URL path they are served from (see /api/media route).
LOCAL_STORAGE_DIR=.storage
LOCAL_STORAGE_PUBLIC_PATH=/uploads

# S3 driver (only needed when STORAGE_DRIVER=s3). For Cloudflare R2, set
# S3_ENDPOINT to https://<account_id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com and region=auto.
S3_ENDPOINT=
S3_REGION=auto
S3_BUCKET=
S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# Public base URL that serves the bucket (CDN / R2 public URL). No trailing slash.
S3_PUBLIC_URL=

# Cloudinary driver (only needed when STORAGE_DRIVER=cloudinary). Easiest:
# paste the "API environment variable" value from the Cloudinary console
# (Dashboard -> Account Details) — it is parsed automatically.
CLOUDINARY_URL=
# …or set the three discrete vars instead (they take precedence if both exist).
CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=
CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=
CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=
# Optional key prefix for all uploaded objects, e.g. "blog". No slashes.
CLOUDINARY_FOLDER=

# ── Rate limiting ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Driver: `memory` (dev / single instance) or `upstash` (prod, serverless-safe).
RATE_LIMIT_DRIVER=memory
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# ── Contact page integrations ─────────────────────────────────
# NeetoCal, behind the /contact "Schedule Meeting" calendar. Server-side only:
# /api/v1/meeting/* proxies it so the key never reaches the browser. Leave the
# key empty and the card links to the NeetoCal booking page instead.
NEETOCAL_API_KEY=
NEETOCAL_BASE_URL=https://softsuave.neetocal.com
NEETOCAL_MEETING_SLUG=meeting-with-softsuave

# Where enquiry and meeting leads are sent when DATABASE_URL is unset: the live
# softsuave.com lead endpoint its own contact forms post to (see
# src/lib/leads/forward.ts). Unset uses that default; override only to point at
# a different collector. With a database configured, leads are stored instead.
# LEAD_FORWARD_URL=https://www.softsuave.com/forms/enquires/developer

# ── First admin (used by `npm run db:seed`) ───────────────────
SEED_ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@example.com
SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD=ChangeMe!2026
SEED_ADMIN_NAME=Site Admin

# ── Security ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Require ADMIN accounts to enable TOTP 2FA (they are redirected to
# /admin/security until they do). Set to "true" to enforce.
ENFORCE_ADMIN_2FA=false

# ── Marketing imagery ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Both are build-time only: the generated files under public/images/ and
# src/lib/home/images.generated.json are committed, so a normal build (CI,
# Vercel) never calls either API and needs neither key.
#
# Pexels fills the slots in content/images.manifest.json that declare no
# `source` — real photography, deduped by photo id across the whole site.
# `npm run images:home`
PEXELS_API_KEY=
# Gemini fills the slots that declare `"source": "gemini"`, from their `prompt`.
# `npm run images:ai` (add `-- --dry-run` to print the prompts and call nothing)
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Optional override — Google renames these faster than this repo ships.
# An `imagen-*` name switches the request to the :predict shape automatically.
GEMINI_IMAGE_MODEL=
